left.raw_text:
Inclusion Criteria:
  -  Adult  [AND] patients who plan to undergo simultaneous primary total knee arthroplasty  [AND] on bilateral knee joint with a diagnosis of osteoarthritis  [OR] or aseptic bone necrosis, [AND]  but not of rheumatoid arthritis;
  -  All patients who have normal preoperative platelet count, normal prothrombin time, normal partial thromboplastin time, [AND]  and normal international normalized ratio;
  -  The use of only balanced electrolyte solutions  [OR] and/or albumin for plasma volume restitution

right.raw_text:
Exclusion Criteria:
  -  Allergy to tranexamic acid;
  -  Receiving warfarin  [OR] or heparin; had a history of hemophilia, [OR]  deep venous thrombosis, [OR]  pulmonary embolism, [OR]  or renal impairment; [OR]  or were pregnant;
  -  Patients with any cardiovascular problems (such as myocardiac infarction history, atrial fibrillation, [OR]  angina);
  -  Patients with thromboembolic disorders, [OR]  or those exhibiting a deteriorating general condition;
  -  Preoperative anemia (a hemoglobin value of <11 g/dL in females  [OR] and <12 g/dL in males), refusal of blood products;
  -  Preoperative use of anticoagulant therapy within five days before surgery, [OR]  fibrinolytic disorders requiring intraoperative antifibrinolytic treatment, [OR]  coagulopathy (as identified by a preoperative platelet count of <150,000/mm3, an international normalized ratio of >1
